  "limits": "One selected authorized attached-viewer capacity refusal and one selected attached-viewer byte-queue overflow are isolated from the same authoritative native TCP and owned-SQLite RunStream execution. The primary RunStream client supplies the exact trusted tool_call and is fully validated, then deliberately disconnected before the selected frame; when the server drops its internal sender is unobserved, and no later disconnected-primary behavior earns release credit. A first authorized GET viewer receives state and remains live while a second authorized GET proves finite capacity refusal without state or terminal. The selected oversized frame then causes the first GET viewer byte-queue overflow detachment. Overflow frees its slot, and a replacement authorized GET viewer receives state containing the trusted tool_call and selected frame exactly once, followed by exact tool_result/done/EOF after callback release. Accepted native publication, held Running/InFlight observations, exact typed/raw histories, an independent durable-result read equal to the replacement terminal result, durable success, orderly retirement, owner+1 reopen and GET-only preservation exclude run cancellation or replay. Fifteen prior targets remain regressions with unchanged receipts. Sixteen scoped proofs and 40 pending scenarios retain open core and COMPAT flags. Disconnected-primary sender behavior, frame-count overflow, all queue sizes, arbitrary backpressure or network splits, cancellation, providers, TypeScript, feature parity and full-workspace behavior are not qualified."
